N+1 happens when you loop items and Laravel runs **1 query for the list + N queries for relations**. Fix it by loading relations **once** using `with()` / `load()` (eager loading). Here’s the real-estate examples you’ll use the most.

---

## 1) The “bad” N+1 example (Properties list)

### ❌ Bad (N+1)

```php
$properties = Property::latest()->paginate(10);

foreach ($properties as $p) {
  echo $p->category->name;  // query each time
  echo $p->agent->name;     // query each time
}
```

### ✅ Good (Eager Loading)

```php
$properties = Property::with(['category', 'agent'])
    ->latest()
    ->paginate(10);
```

---

## 2) Agent dashboard: “My Properties” with category

### ✅ Best practice

```php
$properties = Property::with('category')
    ->ownedBy(auth()->id())     // if you have scope
    ->latest()
    ->paginate(10);
```

Blade:

```blade
{{ $property->category->name }}
```

No extra queries.

---

## 3) Inquiries list (agent side)

You usually show inquiry + property title + user name.

### ❌ Bad (N+1)

```php
$inquiries = Inquiry::where('agent_id', auth()->id())->latest()->paginate(10);

foreach ($inquiries as $i) {
  echo $i->property->title;
  echo $i->user->name;
}
```

### ✅ Good (Eager Loading)

```php
$inquiries = Inquiry::with(['property:id,title', 'user:id,name'])
    ->where('agent_id', auth()->id())
    ->latest()
    ->paginate(10);
```

👉 Notice `property:id,title` and `user:id,name` = loads only needed columns (faster).

---

## 4) Property details page (with images + agent + category)

```php
$property = Property::with([
    'category:id,name',
    'agent:id,name,email,phone',
    'images:id,property_id,image_path,is_primary'
])->findOrFail($id);
```

---

## 5) Use `load()` when you already have the model

```php
$property = Property::findOrFail($id);
$property->load(['category', 'agent', 'images']);
```

---

## 6) Eager load counts (very useful for dashboards)

Example: show each agent’s property count

```php
$agents = User::where('role','agent')
    ->withCount('properties')
    ->get();
```

Blade:

```blade
{{ $agent->properties_count }}
```

---

## 7) Prevent missing relation crashes (optional)

Use null-safe:

```blade
{{ $property->category?->name ?? '-' }}
```

---

## 8) How to detect N+1 quickly (dev tip)

In `AppServiceProvider::boot()`:

```php
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;

public function boot(): void
{
    Model::preventLazyLoading(!app()->isProduction());
}
```

Laravel will warn you when you accidentally create N+1.

---

## Your real estate project “best eager loading sets”

* Properties index: `with(['category','agent'])`
* Agent properties: `with('category')`
* Admin properties: `with(['category','agent'])`
* Inquiries: `with(['property','user'])`
* Property details: `with(['category','agent','images'])`

